## 5. NOTABLE EVENTS
- Motorcyclist carrying a gas cylinder through traffic, min 9
- Red tractor with tanker trailer crossing bottom-right (~30–45s into min 12); red tractor with blue tanker/bowser again at mins 32 and 42
- Woman moving between queued vehicles apparently interacting with occupants, min 29
- Red bus/heavy vehicle entering, min 25
- Police vehicle with red-blue light bar, min 49; white police/traffic van with light bar, min 59
- Road surface turned wet-looking, suggesting recent rain, min 46
- Yellow JCB-type construction vehicle at top right, min 54
- White ambulance in traffic, min 58
- No confirmed accidents or criminal incidents.

## 6. CROWD AND CONGESTION
Severe congestion for nearly the whole hour. Continuous heavy mixed traffic mins 0–24, then continuous severe gridlock — mostly stationary or crawling — mins 25 through 55. Traffic began flowing from min 56 onward. Pedestrian crowd activity within the jam included a man in a blue shirt between vehicles (mins 25, 40, 41, 49), a white-shirt person (mins 25, 36), a man in a light blue shirt standing between lanes (min 50), a woman in green near an auto (min 29), a woman in pink on a scooter (min 30), a man in grey standing among cars (min 47), men with backpacks (min 49), a woman in a black top with maroon backpack crossing (min 57, ~10s), a woman in a red sari crossing top right (min 58, ~20–50s), and a man in a pink shirt and blue jeans crossing centre (min 56, ~51s).

## 7. TRAFFIC VIOLATIONS
Frequent jaywalking by pedestrians crossing on foot between/through the carriageway throughout (multiple minutes, e.g. 25, 29, 30, 36, 40–41, 47, 49, 50, 56–58). No wrong-way driving, helmetless riders, red-light jumping or illegal parking observed.

## 8. PATTERN OF ACTIVITY
The junction was under sustained heavy load for essentially the entire 60 minutes. Mins 0–24: heavy but continuously moving mixed traffic with a steady flow of cars, autos, two-wheelers, goods vehicles and crossing pedestrians. Mins 25–55: full gridlock, stationary/crawling queues, with four-wheelers queuing while two-wheelers filtered between lanes and pedestrians wove through the stationary vehicles; the heaviest and most static period. From min 56 the jam broke and flow resumed. Dominant traffic throughout: white passenger cars, yellow-and-green auto-rickshaws, helmeted motorcyclists and canvas/tarpaulin-covered goods vehicles; oil/cable company trucks and blue tarpaulin three-wheelers recurred during the jam. The pink/red hatchback recurred at mins 20 and 25–55. The scene ended with free-flowing traffic and a police van on site (mins 56–59).

## 9. QUIET PERIODS
None. Even the least congested stretches (mins 0–24, 56–59) carried continuous heavy traffic; no stretch of the footage was quiet.
